          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score more than 36 points (half of 72 total card points) in a deal. First team to reach a target (usually 101) wins.',
          gameplay: "1. **Trump Selection**: Dealer names a suit, No Trump ('Botifarra'), or delegates ('Delegar') to partner. 2. **Doubling**: Opponents can 'Contrar' to double the points. 3. **The Play**: Forehand leads. **Must Follow Suit**. If void, **Must Trump** if the opponent is winning the trick. 4. **Tricks**: Highest trump wins; else highest of led suit.",
          keyRules: [
            'Ranking is A-7-K-J-Q? No, in Botifarra: 9-A-K-Knight-Jack-others.',
            'Jack of Trumps is NOT the boss; the 9 is.',
            "The 'Botifarra' (No Trump) contract doubles the points of the deal automatically.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Protect your 9s and Aces. Since the 9 is worth 5 points, capturing even one is a huge boost. Avoid leading trumps if you are weak.',
          intermediate: "The 'Delegar' Logic: Only delegate to your partner if your hand is perfectly balanced with no strong suits. If you have five cards of one suit, always name it trumps yourself.",
          advanced: "Managing the 'Contrar': Doubling is a psychological tool. Use it not just when you have trumps, but when you suspect the dealer delegated because they have a terrible hand.",
          tips: [
            "Track the 'Manilles' (the four 9s). If all four are out, the Aces become the bosses.",
            "Always try to win the last trick; while it scores no bonus points, it often contains the final 'point' cards.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
