          deckDescription: 'One standard 48-card Spanish deck: twelve ranks (1–12 or equivalent) in each of four suits (coins, cups, swords, batons). No jokers; used for Botifarra (Catalan trick-taking game) where the nine is the highest card and point cards score.',
          suitDescription: 'Four Spanish suits: coins (oros), cups (copas), swords (espadas), and batons (bastos). Trump is determined by the deal or bid; follow suit when able. Each suit has twelve cards; the nine of trump is the manilla (highest).',
          rankDescription: 'Twelve ranks per suit; in Botifarra the nine is highest (5 points), then ace (4), king (3), knight (2), jack (1), others zero. Trick order follows the 48-card Spanish pack; the nine outranks the ace in trump.',
